\": {\"value\": 1.25},\n \"minimum_ratio_q3_q1\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 40, \"max\": null}},\n \"flow_rate_selection_reference\": {\"value\": \"Q3 and ratio Q3/Q1 selected from paragraph 4.1 of OIML R49-1:2013\"}\n}\n\nHmm, the last one is more a note than characteristic. Maybe include, it's informative. Or skip. I'll include the three numeric ones and skip the textual one (it's in table descriptions). Actually \"Q1/Q2 are minimum values; Q3/Q4 are maximum values\" is captured implicitly. Skip.\n\nDo the type_level values need unit_symbol? Dimensionless → null or omit. Shape requires value, unit_symbol? The example shows {\"value\", \"unit_symbol\", \"unit_id\", \"footnote_markers\"}. I'll include unit_symbol: null where relevant. For compactness, \"value\": 1.6, \"unit_symbol\": null.\n\nconfig_level: skip (3D handled by tables + config-qualified models).\n\nShould I ALSO add config_level axis \"bore type and power supply\" listing the three configs? Could add attribute \"configuration\" with three conditions... gimmicky. Skip.\n\nrecommendation: {\"id\": \"R49\", \"edition\": 2013, \"scheme\": \"A\", \"accuracy_classes\": [1, 2]}.\n\nrevision_history: [{\"revision\": \"2\"}].\n\nNow, model_level entries. Write them carefully.\n\nAttribute 1: minimum_flow_q1 (unit m³/h). Values by model id:\n\nRB-BAT-DN40-C12: 0.0625\nRB-BAT-DN50-C12: 0.1\nRB-BAT-DN65-C1: 0.39375\nRB-BAT-DN65-C2: 0.1575\nRB-BAT-DN80-C1: 0.625\nRB-BAT-DN80-C2: 0.25\nRB-BAT-DN100-C1: 1\nRB-BAT-DN100-C2: 0.4\nRB-BAT-DN125-C1: 1\nRB-BAT-DN125-C2: 0.4\nRB-BAT-DN150-C12: 1\nRB-BAT-DN200-C12: 1.575\nRB-BAT-DN250-C1: 6.25\nRB-BAT-DN250-C2: 2.5\nRB-BAT-DN300-C1: 10\nRB-BAT-DN300-C2: 4\nRB-BAT-DN350-C1: 10\nRB-BAT-DN350-C2: 4\nRB-BAT-DN400-C1: 15.625\nRB-BAT-DN400-C2: 12.5\nRB-BAT-DN450-C1: 15.625\nRB-BAT-DN450-C2: 12.5\nRB-BAT-DN500-C1: 100\nRB-BAT-DN500-C2: 40\nRB-BAT-DN600-C1: 157.5\nRB-BAT-DN600-C2: 63\n\nFB-AC-DN40-C12: 0.08\nFB-AC-DN50-C12: 0.126\nFB-AC-DN65-C12: 0.2\nFB-AC-DN80-C12: 0.32\nFB-AC-DN100-